face-image: img/zentrum_3.jpg

= 4295 [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] Conference

The election of Aldwin Stilling to the leadership of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] has stalled any progress toward transforming the party into a true <span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>. His left-leaning stances have alienated potential voters on the dissenting Right, leaving the party adrift—uncertain of its identity. Is it to remain a predominantly Faithful, left-leaning party of labor and social reform, or evolve into a broader, right-of-center *People's Party*?

Despite Stilling himself supporting Sedgewick’s original vision of Faithful unity, he has paradoxically become the chief obstacle in the eyes of the party’s right wing—figures like Sedgewick and Aldermoor now seek to remove him, hoping to steer the party back toward its previous course. However, we retain significant influence within the party’s <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> faction and its affiliated Free Guilds—leverage that could tip the scales back in Stilling’s favor, should we choose to intervene.

- @adenauer: The [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] elects Konrad Aldermoor as the party chair, ousting Stilling.
- @kaiser: Influence the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] to select Aldwin Stilling as the party chair.
- @kaiser_campaign: We will hold a campaign in support of Aldwin Stilling as party chair.

@adenauer
subtitle: The Mayor of Calbridge, and a strong supporter of 'leaving the tower'. Situated on the right-wing of the party.
on-arrival: unionist_relation -= 15; unionist_ideology = "Right"; unionist_leader = "Aldermoor"; commons_unionist -= 6; commons_marcher += 6; disfavored_unionist -= 6; disfavored_marcher += 6; landed_unionist += 6; guild_unionist += 10; landed_traditionalist -= 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; guild_traditionalist -= 8 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; faithful_traditionalist -= 4 if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"; landed_kvp -= 4 if kvp_formed; guild_kvp -= 8 if kvp_formed; faithful_kvp -= 4 if kvp_formed; landed_other -= 4 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; guild_other -= 8 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; faithful_other -= 4 if not kvp_formed and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical"; unionist_party_name = "Concord"; stegerwald_skibidi_time = time + 11
face-image: img/portraits/adenauer.jpg

The influx of dissenting conservatives into the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has rendered Aldwin Stilling’s leadership untenable. In a decisive internal vote of no confidence, Stilling has been ousted—replaced by Sedgewick ally and long-serving Mayor of Calbridge, Konrad Aldermoor. Aldermoor seeks to carry forward Sedgewick’s vision: transforming the party into the dominant force of the Commonwealth Right.

Unsurprisingly, this development has sparked outrage among the <span style="color: #FF7F00;">Faithful Left</span> and Stilling’s supporters, many of whom have resigned their posts in protest. The party’s close ties to left-leaning Free Guilds have been severely strained, plunging the organization into temporary disarray as labor-aligned factions voice their anger. 

Yet despite this internal upheaval, the party remains poised to continue its cannibalization of the fragmented right—especially the beleaguered <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span>. This shift is symbolized by the party's rebranding as the <i>Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>).

[? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": Talks of a merger with the <span style='color: #3E88B3;'>**Traditionalists**</span> are becoming increasingly common—though support is limited to their <span style='color: #0087DC;'>People's Conservatives</span> and <span style='color: #6D5298;'>Faithful Socials</span>. A merger remains impossible without one of those factions having strong, centralized leadership within their party. At the same time, we must prevent any government cooperation between them and the <span style='color: #000000;'>Unionists</span>—lest we allow conditions for such a Free Guild to emerge. ?]

@kaiser
