Through our grassroots connections, and an official campaign, we have somehow managed to secure the reelection of Aldwin Stilling as chairman of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. His removal had once seemed all but inevitable—yet, by some miracle, the present conditions have convinced a majority of the party to rally behind him once more.

As a gesture of compromise, however, Stilling has agreed to officially rename the party to the <i>Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</i> (<span style="color: #000000;">Commonwealth People's Conservative Party</span>). Beyond this cosmetic change—given the historic Faithful association with the '<span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>' label—the party's platform remains largely unchanged.

Even so, this outcome has enraged the party’s right wing. Many of its dissenting conservatives have resigned in protest, retreating to their party of <span class="tooltip-text" title="that's me! the modman!">origin</span>.